{"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles"]]},"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CompatibilityMode","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/GettingStarted"]},{"anchor":"Articles","title":"Articles","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/Architecture","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/ConflictResolution","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CustomCloudBackends"],"generated":true}],"abstract":[{"text":"Transition an existing Ensembles 2 (Objective-C) app to Ensembles 3.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Ensembles 3 is fully backward compatible with Ensembles 2 ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"cloud","type":"text"}]},{"text":" data — existing cloud files and CloudKit records are all readable by E3 out of the box, so a migrated device picks up the rest of the ensemble’s history from the cloud on its first sync. The local event store does not carry across; see ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"What Resets on Migration","type":"text"}]},{"text":" below.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"What’s Backward Compatible","anchor":"Whats-Backward-Compatible","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Cloud files","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — The directory structure and file formats in the cloud are identical. E3 reads all E2 cloud data.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"JSON format","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Property change values use the same JSON serialization.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"CloudKit records","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Record types (","type":"text"},{"code":"CDEFileSystemNode","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"CDEItem","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"CDEDataFile","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") and field names are preserved.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Encryption","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — E3’s ","type":"text"},{"code":".legacy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" encryption format (RNCryptor v3) matches E2’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"CDEEncryptedCloudFileSystem","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Reading E2 data works regardless of compatibility mode — compatibility mode only restricts what E3 ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"exports","type":"text"}]},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"What Resets on Migration","anchor":"What-Resets-on-Migration","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The local event store does ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"not","type":"text"}]},{"text":" carry across. E3 uses a different on-disk database format (raw SQLite vs. E2’s Core Data store), and there is no automatic conversion. On the first call to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/attachPersistentStore(seedPolicy:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" after the swap, E3 deletes the existing event-data directory and registers as a fresh peer with the cloud. Your app’s persistent store (your own Core Data or SwiftData SQLite) is untouched — only Ensembles’ internal event-tracking database is reset.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Practically, this means:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A new ","type":"text"},{"code":"CoreDataEnsemble\/persistentStoreIdentifier","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is generated, so to the cloud and to other peers the migrated device looks like a new device joining the ensemble.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"E3 pulls the current baseline from the cloud and integrates it, so the user’s data ends up consistent with the rest of the ensemble.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Any local events that hadn’t yet synced from E2 are lost. If that matters for your migration window, sync the E2 build to completion before deploying the E3 build.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The first attach also produces a forced detach with ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/EnsembleError\/cloudIdentityChanged","type":"reference"},{"text":" — see step 5 below.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Step-by-Step Migration","anchor":"Step-by-Step-Migration","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"1. Swap the dependency","type":"text"}]}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Replace the Ensembles 2 CocoaPod or framework with the Ensembles 3 Swift package:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ Package.swift",".package(url: \"https:\/\/github.com\/mentalfaculty\/Ensembles-3.git\", from: \"3.0.0\")"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Or add it via Xcode’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add Package Dependencies","type":"text"}]},{"text":" menu.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"2. Set compatibility mode","type":"text"}]}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If some users may still be running the E2 version of your app, set ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CompatibilityMode\/ensembles2Compatible","type":"reference"},{"text":" so E3 restricts its exports to formats E2 peers can parse:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ With a container","let config = EnsembleContainerConfiguration(","    compatibilityMode: .ensembles2Compatible",")","let container = CoreDataEnsembleContainer(","    name: \"MainStore\",","    storeURL: storeURL,","    modelURL: modelURL,","    cloudFileSystem: cloudFS,","    configuration: config",")","","\/\/ Or directly on an ensemble","ensemble.compatibilityMode = .ensembles2Compatible"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"3. Match your existing CloudKit zone (CloudKit users only)","type":"text"}]}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If your existing E2 fleet uses ","type":"text"},{"code":"CloudKitFileSystem","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the most important thing to get right is which initializer you call. Both E2 and E3 expose two private-database initializers, and they pick different CloudKit zones:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Initializer","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Zone","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"init(ubiquityContainerIdentifier:rootDirectory:usePublicDatabase:schemaVersion:)","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"CloudKit’s default zone (","type":"text"},{"code":"_defaultZone","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":")","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"init(privateDatabaseForUbiquityContainerIdentifier:schemaVersion:)","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Custom zone ","type":"text"},{"code":"com.mentalfaculty.ensembles.zone.schema2","type":"codeVoice"}]}]]],"header":"row","type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Your E3 build must use the ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"same initializer","type":"text"}]},{"text":" as the E2 build it is replacing. If the two devices end up in different zones they cannot see each other’s records, even though they are pointed at the same iCloud container with the same schema version. The symptom is ","type":"text"},{"code":"❌ SYNC ERROR Code: 2 - Description: Failed to fetch some records","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on the still-E2 devices, with the repair path’s “Located some items in CloudKit without data” log.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To find out which zone your E2 fleet is on, look at the ","type":"text"},{"code":"CDECloudKitFileSystem","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" init in your existing E2 source. If it calls ","type":"text"},{"code":"initWithUbiquityContainerIdentifier:rootDirectory:usePublicDatabase:schemaVersion:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", you’re on the default zone — call the matching E3 init. If it calls ","type":"text"},{"code":"initWithPrivateDatabaseForUbiquityContainerIdentifier:schemaVersion:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", you’re on the custom zone — call the matching E3 init. Don’t switch initializers as part of the migration; switch only after the entire fleet is on E3.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"4. Update API names","type":"text"}]}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Ensembles 3 uses different class and method names:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Ensembles 2 (Objective-C)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Ensembles 3 (Swift)","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"CDEPersistentStoreEnsemble","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble","type":"reference"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"CDEPersistentStoreEnsembleDelegate","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleDelegate","type":"reference"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"leechPersistentStore(...)","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"CoreDataEnsemble\/attachPersistentStore()","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"deleechPersistentStore(...)","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/detachPersistentStore()","type":"reference"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"mergeWithCompletion:","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/sync(options:)","type":"reference"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"CDECloudFileSystem","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CloudFileSystem","type":"reference"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"CDEEncryptedCloudFileSystem","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"EncryptedCloudFileSystem","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"CDECloudKitFileSystem","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"CloudKitFileSystem","type":"codeVoice"}]}]]],"header":"row","type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"5. Handle the first-launch identity detach","type":"text"}]}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"On the first launch after migrating from E2, expect a forced detach with ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/EnsembleError\/cloudIdentityChanged","type":"reference"},{"text":" (code 202). The first attach in E3 wipes the existing E2 event store and registers a fresh peer, but the cached cloud identity token is not carried across either. The first identity check after attach sees no stored token, treats it as an account change, and forces a detach.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Re-attaching immediately captures the current identity and steady state resumes. If your app responds to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleDelegate\/coreDataEnsemble(_:didDetachWithError:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" by disabling sync, every migrating user will silently lose sync until they toggle it back on. Handle this case explicitly:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["func coreDataEnsemble(","    _ ensemble: CoreDataEnsemble,","    didDetachWithError error: Error",") {","    if let error = error as? EnsembleError, error == .cloudIdentityChanged {","        \/\/ First launch after E2 → E3 migration, or a real account change.","        \/\/ Re-attach rather than disabling sync.","        Task {","            try? await Task.sleep(for: .seconds(1))","            try? await ensemble.attachPersistentStore()","        }","        return","    }","    \/\/ Other errors: disable sync and surface to the user.","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The same pattern applies to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/EnsembleError\/hardwareIdentityChanged","type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/EnsembleError\/storeUnregistered","type":"reference"},{"text":" in general — all three are recoverable by re-attaching. Errors like ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/EnsembleError\/dataCorruptionDetected","type":"reference"},{"text":" do warrant disabling sync until the user intervenes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"6. Test thoroughly","type":"text"}]}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Verify your app can read existing cloud data from E2 peers.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Confirm that E2 peers can still read data exported by your E3 build (while in ","type":"text"},{"code":".ensembles2Compatible","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" mode).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Test attachment, sync, and detach cycles.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Test the first-launch reset on a device that previously ran E2 — including the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/EnsembleError\/cloudIdentityChanged","type":"reference"},{"text":" recovery path.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"7. Switch to full E3 mode","type":"text"}]}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Once all users have upgraded to the E3 version of your app, change the compatibility mode to unlock future E3-only features:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["ensemble.compatibilityMode = .ensembles3  \/\/ the default"]},{"level":3,"text":"What `ensembles2Compatible` Restricts","anchor":"What-ensembles2Compatible-Restricts","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Currently, ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CompatibilityMode\/ensembles2Compatible","type":"reference"},{"text":" applies one restriction:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Model hashes","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Forces ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/compressModelHashes","type":"reference"},{"text":" to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":", so model version hashes use the full XML property list format that E2 peers can parse."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"No other export behavior is changed. As E3 evolves, additional restrictions may be added to this mode to maintain E2 compatibility.","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ensembles\/migratingfromensembles2"]}],"metadata":{"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Migrating from Ensembles 2","modules":[{"name":"Ensembles"}]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/MigratingFromEnsembles2","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/CustomCloudBackends":{"title":"Custom Cloud Backends","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CustomCloudBackends","abstract":[{"text":"Implement the CloudFileSystem protocol to sync via any storage service.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/customcloudbackends","kind":"article"},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/CompatibilityMode":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CompatibilityMode","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/compatibilitymode","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"CompatibilityMode","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"to